<title>POLAND: Polish broad money rises 1.1 pct in May 1-10.</title>
<headline>Polish broad money rises 1.1 pct in May 1-10.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's broad money rose by 1.62 billion zlotys, or 1.1 percent, in May 1-10 to 146.41 billion after a 2.3 percent rise in April, preliminary central bank figures showed.</p>
<p>Broad money supply grew 7.9 percent in the January-May 10 period.  </p>
<p> BROAD POLISH MONEY		    MAY 1-10     APRIL   MAY '96</p>
<p>  month/month change (pct)		1.1	  2.3	 1.6</p>
<p>  Money in bln zlotys		   146.41     144.80    115.27</p>
<p>  Foreign currency (in bln PLN)	25.36	25.36     21.47</p>
<p>  National currency		     121.05     119.44     93.80</p>
<p>  Cash in circulation		    26.33	25.86     21.83</p>
<p>  Lending to non-financial sector    90.68	90.29     61.82</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
